      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm an architect and i've been living in one of the new high-tech developments in hudson yards for a few months now. i've been noticing this weird, low-frequency hum coming from the smart HVAC and integrated lighting systems. it's not something you can really hear, but it's like a constant pressure in my chest and it's making me feel incredibly anxious and restless for no reason. i've been looking into architectural psychoacoustics and i'm starting to suspect these frequencies are being modulated on purpose. do you know anything about how smart building systems can be used to influence occupant mood or behavior through sub-audible frequencies?",
